Introduction:
Bubble sort is a simple sorting algorithm that is used to sort an array of integers in ascending or descending order. It is called bubble sort because the smaller values "bubble" to the top of the array while the larger values "sink" to the bottom. Bubble sort is efficient for small datasets but its time complexity is O(n^2) which makes it inefficient for large datasets. 

